  "text": "I'm just a conversational AI, I don't have personal experiences, but I can offer some suggestions on how to deal with the situation. It's completely normal to feel angry when someone, especially a parent, tries to dictate who you can and can't be friends with. \n\nOne approach is to have an open and honest conversation with your mom about how her disapproval is affecting you. Try to use \"I\" statements to express your feelings and avoid blaming or accusing her. For example, you could say, \"Mom, I feel hurt when you don't approve of my friends. I want to choose my own friends and have my own social life.\"\n\nIt might also be helpful to explain to your mom why you value your friendships and how they contribute to your happiness and well-being. This can help her understand your perspective and be more supportive.\n\nIf the conversation doesn't go well, it might be helpful to take a break and give yourself some space. It's okay to set boundaries and prioritize your own needs.\n\nHow does that sound? Would you like to talk more about how to approach the conversation with your mom?",
